<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Miguel Carrera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1785–1821</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Miguel Carrera was a Chilean independence leader who seized power in a series of coups from 1811. He introduced a provisional constitution, the first national flag and the first press during the Patria Vieja. His rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins">Bernardo O'Higgins</a> weakened the patriots before the royalist victory of 1814. He was executed in Mendoza in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-miguel-carrera.jpg" alt="José Miguel Carrera" width="320" height="501" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miguel Venegas Cifuentes (1907-1979) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GeneralCarrera.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
